{%- comment -%}
  snippets/portal-chrome.liquid — the portal's entry point and its only gate
  (spec tasks 19.1 and 19.3, design §25.2, §17.3, §17.4).

  Requirements 4.12, 17.3, 17.4, 17.8, 17.10, 22.1, 22.2, 22.3, 22.10, 25.6, 25.9.

  ── THE FLAG IS EVALUATED HERE, ONCE ──────────────────────────────────────────
  §25.2 requires the flag to be read server-side BEFORE any portal markup exists,
  so that with it off the response is byte-identical to today's. That is only
  checkable if there is one place it happens. Every page template renders this
  snippet and nothing else, so the ten templates cannot drift into ten different
  gate conditions.

  A `{% render %}`d snippet has an isolated scope and cannot hand a variable back
  to its caller, which is exactly why the gate lives in the snippet rather than in
  the templates: there is no way to compute `portal_on` in one place and consume it
  in ten without `{% include %}`, which Shopify has deprecated.

  ── THE THREE BRANCHES, IN ORDER ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    1. flag off      -> the page's own admin-authored content, and nothing else.
                        No portal markup, no stylesheet, no script tag.
    2. no customer   -> `portal-signin-invitation` only (task 19.2). An anonymous
                        visitor gets no shell, no data hooks and no portal script.
    3. signed in     -> the chrome, the navigation, and the requested section.

  Branch 1 renders `page.content` rather than nothing because these are real
  Shopify pages: whatever the merchant typed in the admin is the honest "not
  available yet" state, and it leaks nothing about the portal's existence.

  ── WHY THERE IS NO SECOND `<main>` AND NO SECOND SKIP LINK ───────────────────
  Task 19.1 asks for "one `<main>` ... and a skip link as the first focusable
  element". The theme already provides both: `layout/theme.liquid:350` renders
  `<main id="MainContent" role="main">` around `content_for_layout`, and line 325
  renders the skip link that targets it. Because this snippet renders INSIDE that
  `<main>`, adding another would put two `main` landmarks on the page — a WCAG 1.3.1
  failure — and a second skip link would add a focus stop that duplicates the
  first. So the requirement is met by the theme's elements, unchanged.

  What the theme does NOT provide is a way past the account navigation: a keyboard
  user who follows the site skip link lands before the rail and must traverse eight
  entries to reach the content. The portal therefore adds ONE internal skip link as
  the first focusable element within itself. That is additive, and it is the actual
  barrier §20.2 is about.

  ── ASSETS ARE INCLUDED PER PAGE, NOT IN THE LAYOUT ───────────────────────────
  The stylesheet and the two scripts are emitted here, inside the flag. §25.6
  requires the `<head>` asset list of every other page to be unchanged, and the
  cheapest way to guarantee that is never to touch `layout/theme.liquid` at all —
  which also means an anonymous visitor and a flag-off visitor download none of it.
  `templates/page.wishlist.liquid` sets the same precedent in this theme.

  PARAMETERS
    section_name  the `data-portal-section` value, e.g. `orders`
    page_title    the visible page title
    nav_key       which navigation entry is current; defaults to `section_name`
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign portal_on = false
  if settings.portal_enabled
    assign portal_on = true
  elsif settings.portal_allowlist != blank and customer
    assign needle = ',' | append: customer.id | append: ','
    assign hay = ',' | append: settings.portal_allowlist | append: ','
    assign hay = hay | replace: ' ', ''
    if hay contains needle
      assign portal_on = true
    endif
  endif

  assign nav_current = nav_key | default: section_name
-%}

{%- if portal_on -%}
  {%- if customer -%}
    {{ 'athoor-portal.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    <div class="athoor-portal" data-portal-root>
      {%- comment -%}
        The first focusable element inside the portal. Skips the rail, not the page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a class="athoor-portal__skip" href="#AthoorPortalContent">Skip to {{ page_title | default: 'account' | downcase }}</a>

      {%- comment -%}
        ONE global live region for cross-section confirmations (§20.6). It is
        server-rendered because a region injected at announcement time is not
        reliably announced.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="athoor-portal__live" data-portal-live-global role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

      <header class="athoor-portal__header">
        <p class="athoor-portal__wordmark">MY ATHOOR</p>
        <h1 class="athoor-portal__title">{{ page_title | default: 'Your account' }}</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="athoor-portal__body">
        {% render 'portal-nav', current: nav_current %}

        <div class="athoor-portal__content" id="AthoorPortalContent" tabindex="-1">
          {{ content }}
        </div>
      </div>

      <footer class="athoor-portal__footer">
        <a class="athoor-portal__footer-link" href="{{ routes.account_logout_url }}">Sign out</a>
      </footer>

      {% render 'portal-more-sheet', current: nav_current %}
    </div>

    <script src="{{ 'athoor-portal-core.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- if section_name != blank -%}
      <script src="{{ 'athoor-portal-' | append: section_name | append: '.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {% render 'portal-signin-invitation' %}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  {{ page.content }}
{%- endif -%}
